 {"id": "DB-GAP-059", "title": "Integration suite leaks ORPHANED scratch daemons (2 found live: :33523 + :30720, 3.7/3.9GB RSS, 41% CPU each, ~10k FDs each, 20k scratch files) — detached spawn with no process-level reaper + an unbounded (un-timed) test probe", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "complexity": 3, "created_by": "kara-foreman-direct", "created_at": "2026-09-25", "detail": "FOUND LIVE 2026-09-25 by host audit: two ORPHANED test-spawned daemons running at once — pid 1933499 (:33523, 2h13m, 3.7GB RSS, 10950 FDs, 10937 scratch files) and pid 3427633 (:30720, 1h34m, 3.9GB RSS, 9271 FDs, 9261 scratch files). 41% CPU each (2 cores burned), /tmp 257MB -> 21MB after cleanup, and NEITHER died on SIGTERM (event loop starved) — SIGKILL + ProcessGroup kill needed. Their hung parent tree was killed with them: bash /tmp/db590_intretry.sh -> npm exec vitest run --config vitest.integration.config.ts (isolated at the 'RUN v5.0.1' banner for 1h34m, zero test output) plus two stuck probes `curl -s -D - http://127.0.0.1:<port>/users` (parents long dead). MECHANISM — three compounding defects: (1) tests/helpers.ts startDuckbrainHttp spawns each scratch daemon detached:true, so it owns its process group and SURVIVES its spawner; the only reaper is killProcess in the file's afterAll, which never runs when a run is hard-killed or stalls => the daemon reparents to systemd --user and lives forever. The repo's sweepOrphanScratchFiles reclaims only FILES whose pid is dead; nothing ever reclaims an orphaned PROCESS. (2) tests/helpers.ts curl() (~line 266) runs `curl -s -D - <args>` with NO --max-time, unlike waitForUrl which got --max-time 10 in INT-CI-003 — so a stalled request pins the suite forever rather than failing and letting teardown run; tests/http-e2e.int.test.ts ('should respond to /users with authors array') is the call site that hung. (3) GET /users walks whatever namespace root the daemon inherited — startDuckbrainHttp sets only DUCKBRAIN_EMBEDDING_*, so a scratch daemon reads the HOST config (227 real namespaces) — doing per-namespace `git log --all --format=%aN` + a DuckDB singleton connection whose CONNECTION_MAX_AGE_MS=1h expiry forces a RECYCLE on every pass, and getSingletonConnection opens a FRESH scratch file per recycle (duckbrain-<pid>-<hash>-<n>.db, counter++). Result: unbounded FD + file churn (1.4 files/s sustained) = GB-scale RSS, 41% CPU, and a request that never answers. FIX SHAPE: (a) bound the test probe with --max-time (mirror INT-CI-003) so a stalled daemon fails the test instead of hanging it; (b) give scratch daemons a reaper that survives a hard-killed parent (parent-death detection / startup sweep of orphaned duckbrain http --port= processes, not just their files) — and note HANDLE-vs-FILE: closeEntry's unlink is fire-and-forget after db.close(), which never completes in a starved loop; (c) pin an isolated namespace root + port for scratch daemons so an integration file can neither walk nor depend on the production store. EVIDENCE: reaper log ~/.hermes/logs/stray-duckbrain-reaper.jsonl; journal 10:18:23/10:18:31; SIGTERM-survival recorded on both pids. HOST GUARD ALREADY ARMED (host-side, not a repo fix): ~/.hermes/scripts/stray-duckbrain-reaper.py + stray-duckbrain-reaper.timer (60s) — kills only processes that are daemon-shaped AND orphaned AND not the managed unit (MainPID/ControlGroup, never the cgroup leaf: agent terminals run inside hermes-gateway.service, so a leaf test wrongly classifies worker-spawned strays as managed) AND on a non-managed port, then reclaims their scratch files.", "commit_hash": "80b8923", "worker_summary": "Worker fixed three defects: (a) curl probes bounded with --max-time 10 (CURL_MAX_TIME_S=10), (b) orphaned scratch-daemon reaper added (src/testing/orphan-daemon-reaper.ts) with globalSetup/teardown sweeps in global-setup.integration.ts, (c) startDuckbrainHttp pins DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACES_PATH, DUCKBRAIN_DATA_DIR, DUCKBRAIN_CONFIG_PATH to isolated temp dirs. Files: tests/helpers.ts, tests/global-setup.integration.ts, tests/http-e2e.int.test.ts, src/testing/orphan-daemon-reaper.ts, src/testing/orphan-daemon-reaper.test.ts, tests/orphan-reaper.int.test.ts. Judge PASS tier1 740a72fa (tier2 skipped - judge timeout).", "foreman_note": "Foreman tick 629: picked DB-GAP-059 (P2, orphaned scratch daemons). Work committed as 80b8923 on origin/main. Tier1 judge PASS. Tier2 skipped (judge timeout)."}
